topIssues.body:
Parent epic: #17175

Implement household coordination on the existing EntityStore/RelationshipStore, approval queue, audit ledger, and scheduler.

Acceptance criteria:
- typed roles cover owner, co-parent, partner, caregiver, child, and professional without assuming one default parent;
- grants distinguish free/busy, event detail, propose, approve, mutate, and export scopes with expiry/revocation;
- schedule proposals and accepted agreements are distinct immutable versions;
- affected adults approve material changes and stale approvals are invalidated;
- custody/holiday exceptions and concurrent proposals resolve deterministically without leaking private details;
- append-only audit and scoped export show source, actor, decision, version, approval, and outcome;
- real PGlite tests cover revoked caregivers, co-parent privacy, concurrent proposals, stale approval, and export redaction.

Do not add a second household graph or scheduler.

Parent epic: #17175

Replace direct negotiation-side connector sends with a fail-closed approval and receipt rail.

Acceptance criteria:
- start/propose/finalize/cancel persist exact outbound drafts and never dispatch directly;
- approval binds recipient, channel, subject/body bytes, negotiation/proposal version, and content hash;
- state mutation plus approval/outbox is atomic, idempotent, and race-safe;
- execution revalidates current negotiation, proposal, affected parties, and material changes;
- approved sends use provider idempotency keys and persist typed attempts/receipts before reporting completion;
- retries cannot duplicate external messages and provider ambiguity remains visibly unresolved;
- cross-subject access, tampering, stale approvals, concurrent enqueue, queue failure, and all supported transports are covered with PGlite/provider-seam tests.

Mocks alone do not close this issue; attach sandbox/live connector receipts and reviewed logs.

Parent epic: #17175

Implement the calendar truth foundation required before family scheduling can make availability claims.

Acceptance criteria:
- preserve connector account and grant identity for calendars, events, sync state, and pruning;
- drain Google calendar/event pages and persist incremental sync tokens per account/calendar;
- recover expired cursors with a full snapshot and apply cancellation tombstones without cross-account deletion;
- preserve attendee RSVP/role, transparency, visibility, and explicit send-update semantics;
- expose complete/partial/unavailable source health so missing data never reads as free time;
- provide privacy-only guest free/busy and deterministic conflict evaluation;
- prove multi-account isolation, partial failure, cursor deltas, 410 recovery, DST/all-day/tentative/declined/private-busy behavior with automated tests.

Evidence must include real provider or sandbox-provider logs and domain artifacts; mocks alone do not close this issue.
